\ Fourth Genstat reference program for predictmeans: likelihood ratio tests
\ of variance components for varcomp(test = TRUE) (R/vc-test.R). Each model is
\ fitted in full and reduced form; the change in REML deviance is the LRT.
\ Please save the whole Output window (File > Save) and send that file; the
\ first run may need small syntax fixes. Cases: (1) Oats split plot, complete
\ (72 plots): Block and Block.Variety variances; (2) Orthodont: random
\ intercept and uncorrelated random slope of age; (3) Orthodont: random
\ intercept with AR(1) between the four ages of each child, and without.

\ ---- 1. Oats: 6 blocks x 3 varieties x 4 nitrogen levels, complete ----
UNITS [NVALUES=72]
FACTOR [LEVELS=6] Block
FACTOR [LABELS=!t(GoldenRain, Marvellous, Victory)] Variety
FACTOR [LEVELS=!(0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6)] Nitro
VARIATE Yield
READ Block, Variety, Nitro, Yield
1 3 0.0 111   1 3 0.2 130   1 3 0.4 157   1 3 0.6 174
1 1 0.0 117   1 1 0.2 114   1 1 0.4 161   1 1 0.6 141
1 2 0.0 105   1 2 0.2 140   1 2 0.4 118   1 2 0.6 156
2 3 0.0 61   2 3 0.2 91   2 3 0.4 97   2 3 0.6 100
2 1 0.0 70   2 1 0.2 108   2 1 0.4 126   2 1 0.6 149
2 2 0.0 96   2 2 0.2 124   2 2 0.4 121   2 2 0.6 144
3 3 0.0 68   3 3 0.2 64   3 3 0.4 112   3 3 0.6 86
3 1 0.0 60   3 1 0.2 102   3 1 0.4 89   3 1 0.6 96
3 2 0.0 89   3 2 0.2 129   3 2 0.4 132   3 2 0.6 124
4 3 0.0 74   4 3 0.2 89   4 3 0.4 81   4 3 0.6 122
4 1 0.0 64   4 1 0.2 103   4 1 0.4 132   4 1 0.6 133
4 2 0.0 70   4 2 0.2 89   4 2 0.4 104   4 2 0.6 117
5 3 0.0 62   5 3 0.2 90   5 3 0.4 100   5 3 0.6 116
5 1 0.0 80   5 1 0.2 82   5 1 0.4 94   5 1 0.6 126
5 2 0.0 63   5 2 0.2 70   5 2 0.4 109   5 2 0.6 99
6 3 0.0 53   6 3 0.2 74   6 3 0.4 118   6 3 0.6 113
6 1 0.0 89   6 1 0.2 82   6 1 0.4 86   6 1 0.6 104
6 2 0.0 97   6 2 0.2 99   6 2 0.4 119   6 2 0.6 121
:
\ (1a) full: random Block and Block.Variety
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Variety*Nitro] RANDOM=Block/Variety
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] Yield
\ (1b) Block.Variety dropped
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Variety*Nitro] RANDOM=Block
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] Yield
\ (1c) Block dropped
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=Variety*Nitro] RANDOM=Block.Variety
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] Yield

\ ---- 2 and 3. Orthodont: 27 children x 4 ages (8, 10, 12, 14) ----
UNITS [NVALUES=108]
FACTOR [LEVELS=27] Subject
FACTOR [LEVELS=4] Occ
VARIATE age, distance
READ Subject, Occ, age, distance
1 1 8 26   1 2 10 25   1 3 12 29   1 4 14 31
2 1 8 21.5   2 2 10 22.5   2 3 12 23   2 4 14 26.5
3 1 8 23   3 2 10 22.5   3 3 12 24   3 4 14 27.5
4 1 8 25.5   4 2 10 27.5   4 3 12 26.5   4 4 14 27
5 1 8 20   5 2 10 23.5   5 3 12 22.5   5 4 14 26
6 1 8 24.5   6 2 10 25.5   6 3 12 27   6 4 14 28.5
7 1 8 22   7 2 10 22   7 3 12 24.5   7 4 14 26.5
8 1 8 24   8 2 10 21.5   8 3 12 24.5   8 4 14 25.5
9 1 8 23   9 2 10 20.5   9 3 12 31   9 4 14 26
10 1 8 27.5   10 2 10 28   10 3 12 31   10 4 14 31.5
11 1 8 23   11 2 10 23   11 3 12 23.5   11 4 14 25
12 1 8 21.5   12 2 10 23.5   12 3 12 24   12 4 14 28
13 1 8 17   13 2 10 24.5   13 3 12 26   13 4 14 29.5
14 1 8 22.5   14 2 10 25.5   14 3 12 25.5   14 4 14 26
15 1 8 23   15 2 10 24.5   15 3 12 26   15 4 14 30
16 1 8 22   16 2 10 21.5   16 3 12 23.5   16 4 14 25
17 1 8 21   17 2 10 20   17 3 12 21.5   17 4 14 23
18 1 8 21   18 2 10 21.5   18 3 12 24   18 4 14 25.5
19 1 8 20.5   19 2 10 24   19 3 12 24.5   19 4 14 26
20 1 8 23.5   20 2 10 24.5   20 3 12 25   20 4 14 26.5
21 1 8 21.5   21 2 10 23   21 3 12 22.5   21 4 14 23.5
22 1 8 20   22 2 10 21   22 3 12 21   22 4 14 22.5
23 1 8 21.5   23 2 10 22.5   23 3 12 23   23 4 14 25
24 1 8 23   24 2 10 23   24 3 12 23.5   24 4 14 24
25 1 8 20   25 2 10 21   25 3 12 22   25 4 14 21.5
26 1 8 16.5   26 2 10 19   26 3 12 19   26 4 14 19.5
27 1 8 24.5   27 2 10 25   27 3 12 28   27 4 14 28
:
\ (2a) random intercept and uncorrelated random slope (lmer: age || Subject)
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject + Subject.age
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] distance
\ (2b) slope dropped
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] distance
\ (2c) intercept dropped, slope kept
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject.age
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] distance
\ (3a) random intercept; AR(1) between the ages of each child
VCOMPONENTS [FIXED=age] RANDOM=Subject + Subject.Occ
VSTRUCTURE [TERMS=Subject.Occ] FACTOR=Occ; MODEL=AR; ORDER=1
REML [PRINT=model, components, deviance; METHOD=AI] distance
\ (3b) the same with the AR(1) correlation 0 (independent residuals): (2b)
STOP
